   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 2024472,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 367747,
    "poster_id": 67223,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > be an integer greater than <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Define<br>\n<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524fd235d6d0516c162ff6f260072fa01c69dc13.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1 = n, y_1 = 1, x_{i+1} =\\left[ \\frac{x_i+y_i}{2}\\right] , y_{i+1} = \\left[ \\frac{n}{x_{i+1}}\\right], \\qquad \\text{for }i = 1, 2, \\ldots\\ ,\\]\"  width=\"539\" height=\"43\" ><br>\n<br>\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d87c4df7a861f6bc1a1be5600dcf4111c49841.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[z]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" > denotes the largest integer less than or equal to <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"8\" >.</span> Prove that<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfea1c36fea1237d468e3f8863bd14041d48fe40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\min \\{x_1, x_2, \\ldots,  x_n \\} =[ \\sqrt n ]\\]\"  width=\"210\" height=\"20\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Let $n$ be an integer greater than $1$. Define\n\n\\[x_1 = n, y_1 = 1, x_{i+1} =\\left[ \\frac{x_i+y_i}{2}\\right] , y_{i+1} = \\left[ \\frac{n}{x_{i+1}}\\right], \\qquad \\text{for }i = 1, 2, \\ldots\\ ,\\]\n\nwhere $[z]$ denotes the largest integer less than or equal to $z$. Prove that\n\\[ \\min \\{x_1, x_2, \\ldots,  x_n \\} =[ \\sqrt n ]\\]",
    "username": "Amir Hossein",
    "post_number": 1,
    "post_format": "bbcode",
